Bundle-Name: Model Atlas GDPR Metadata Diagnostics
Bundle-Description: Writes the findings of a GDPR review onto the metadata of the model the \
 review is about, as Diagnostics under the producer 'gdpr.review'. Opening the schema registry \
 then tells a package that was found to hold special-category data from one that was found clean.

# In model.atlas rather than in fennec-gdpr, for the reason the history bundle gives: the
# feature has to work in a deployment that has no AI review half, where a human uploads a
# report by hand. Nothing here depends on fennec-gdpr - the GdprReport EPackage lives in
# common.models - and nothing here changes gdpr-report.ecore, which is a shared model that
# knows nothing of Atlas topology.
#
# Sibling of org.eclipse.fennec.model.atlas.gdpr.history, not part of it: one action, one
# output. Both run off the same event with onFailure 'continue', so a failing metadata write
# never costs a document rebuild, and a deployment may want either without the other.
#
# Everything that reads the report is in GdprFindingsToDiagnostics, a pure function with no
# OSGi and no storage. The stage action is the thin part.

-workingset: ModelAtlas

-library: enableEMF

-buildpath: \
	org.eclipse.fennec.gdpr.report.model;version=latest,\
	org.eclipse.fennec.model.atlas.action.api;version=snapshot,\
	org.eclipse.fennec.model.atlas.scope.api;version=snapshot,\
	org.eclipse.fennec.model.atlas.workflow;version=snapshot,\
	org.eclipse.fennec.model.atlas.management;version=snapshot,\
	org.osgi.util.promise;version=latest,\
	org.osgi.service.component;version=latest,\
	org.osgi.service.metatype.annotations;version=latest

-testpath: junit-jupiter-api

-privatepackage: org.eclipse.fennec.model.atlas.gdpr.diagnostics

Bundle-Version: 1.0.0.SNAPSHOT
